# Secure User Management API
## Project Documentation & Development Roadmap

**Technology Stack:** Node.js, TypeScript, Express.js, PostgreSQL, JWT  
**Project Type:** REST API  
**Current Status:** Step 3 – PostgreSQL Integration Completed  
**Purpose:** Learning, practical backend development, portfolio, and interview preparation.

---

# 1. Project Overview

The Secure User Management API is a backend application designed to manage users securely.

The application will support user registration, login, email verification, profile management, authentication, authorization, and administrative user management.

The project is being developed step by step using industry-standard backend development practices.

## 1.1 Main Objectives

1. Build a REST API using Node.js, TypeScript, and Express.
2. Store application data in PostgreSQL.
3. Implement secure user registration and login.
4. Implement email verification during registration.
5. Implement JWT-based authentication.
6. Implement role-based authorization.
7. Allow administrators to manage users.
8. Maintain a consistent API response structure.
9. Handle errors centrally.
10. Understand how to design an API that can handle high traffic, including a target scenario of 100,000 simultaneous requests.

# 2. Technology Stack

| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Node.js | JavaScript runtime for backend development |
| TypeScript | Static typing and better code maintainability |
| Express.js | Backend web framework |
| PostgreSQL | Relational database |
| pg | Node.js PostgreSQL driver |
| JWT | Authentication tokens |
| Argon2id | Secure password hashing |
| Zod | Request validation |
| Nodemailer | Sending emails |
| Redis | Caching and shared data |
| BullMQ | Background job processing |
| Git | Version control |
| Vitest / Supertest | Testing |

Some technologies will be introduced in later development stages.

